I come home.
I knock on Nina's door.
Nina opens and smiles.
"How is it going?" asks Nina.
"It is going well," I answer.
"I have a Danish phone number now."
I give Nina my new number.
She types it into her phone.
"And my number is eighty-seven, sixty-five, forty-three, twenty-one," she says.
I save her number on my phone.
Now we have each other's numbers.
We are neighbours.
Now we are also friends.
